<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bond prices closed firmer on comments by Joaquim Molins, parliamentary spokesman for the Catalan nationalists, that there was broad agreement on the 1997 budget with the ruling Popular Party.</p>
<p>Markets were also helped by the government's repeated message that the budget would be firm and would help Spain meet the Maastricht convergence criteria for European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;Without a doubt, all these comments create a favourable environment in the market,&quot; said a trader.</p>
</text>
